{
  "_comment_READ_ME_FIRST": [
    "This is a BEST-EFFORT template, not a verified schema dump. R4 confirmed the Codex HOOK EVENT MODEL",
    "(event names, PreCompact/PostCompact's manual|auto matcher, SessionStart's source values, the",
    "continue:false PreCompact veto) against documentation and a live app-server probe — see",
    "adapters/codex/README.md, 'What is verified vs. what is templated'. The exact JSON KEYS a",
    "hooks.json registration entry uses (this file's 'hooks'/'matcher'/'command' names) were NOT",
    "independently confirmed against a live, trusted Codex hooks install in this task. Treat every key",
    "name here as a documented-shape best guess modelled on the same command-array convention Claude",
    "Code's own hooks.json uses (the two hosts share the same event-name vocabulary throughout the R4",
    "verification, which is the basis for the guess) — verify against your installed Codex CLI's own",
    "current schema (its own docs, or a `codex hooks` subcommand if one exists in your version) before",
    "trusting this file to be syntactically exact.",
    "",
    "WHAT ACTUALLY PROVES THIS WORKED: not this file parsing without error. The activation canary",
    "(respawnpack-canary.js) writes .respawnpack/runtime/rollover/_codex-hooks-canary.json only when a",
    "registered, TRUSTED hook actually fires. Installed-but-untrusted, or installed-but-wrong-schema,",
    "both read as CANNOT_DETERMINE in adapters/codex/profile.js until that marker exists and is fresh.",
    "",
    "TRUST STEP (loud, on purpose): registering these hooks is NOT enough. Codex gates hooks on BOTH",
    "`features.hooks` (a feature flag) AND a PER-HOOK interactive trust decision made with `/hooks` inside",
    "a live Codex session. Until you run `/hooks` and approve each entry below, Codex will not run them —",
    "and there is no scriptable way to list which hooks are currently trusted, so the canary marker is the",
    "only after-the-fact proof. An installed-but-never-approved hook is CANNOT_DETERMINE, never 'active'.",
    "",
    "PLACEHOLDER: replace every {{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}} below with the ABSOLUTE path to this",
    "adapter's hooks/ directory (typically <install-root>/adapters/codex/hooks). Installer/uninstaller",
    "wiring is DEFERRED past this task — see adapters/codex/README.md, 'What the installer wave must add'.",
    "",
    "This file is JSON, so these notes live in throwaway '_comment_*' keys rather than real comments.",
    "STRIP every '_comment_*' key before this is merged into a real ~/.codex/hooks.json or <repo>/.codex/",
    "hooks.json — they document the template, they are not hook registrations, and a strict parser may",
    "not tolerate them sitting inside the 'hooks' object as-is."
  ],

  "hooks": {
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "manual|auto",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-precompact.js\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "manual|auto",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-postcompact.js\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-canary.js\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-sessionstart.js\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-canary.js\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-stop.js\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "node \"{{RESPAWNPACK_CODEX_HOOKS_DIR}}/respawnpack-canary.js\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "_comment_canary_breadth": [
      "The canary (respawnpack-canary.js) is safe to register against ANY event, including",
      "permission-sensitive ones, because it NEVER emits a decision — see its own file header. Registering",
      "it more broadly than the four events above (e.g. also under PreToolUse, PermissionRequest,",
      "PostToolUse, UserPromptSubmit, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, SessionEnd) makes the activation-proof",
      "marker refresh as soon as ANY one of your trusted hooks fires, which is the more robust posture",
      "given Codex's per-hook (not per-project) trust model. Left out of the default template only to keep",
      "the first-install trust prompt from `/hooks` short; add rows for the events you actually trust."
    ]
  }
}
